\\ sparks.6502 - the ring of particles a merge throws out (P21), as sparks.py does it, after the original's:
\\ a spark each way of 8 from the new ball's edge (sparkthrow.6502), slowing by 1/8 a frame, drifting
\\ down if gravity's on, and gone after 13 to 20 frames (the shrinking white ball's, 3: D31) or on leaving
\\ the well. Each is a pixel two lines tall in the ball's colours.
\\
\\ Each frame, after the balls, every spark is EORed off with what it was EORed on with last frame, moved,
\\ and EORed on with (the byte EOR its colour) AND its pixel's mask, which it keeps. So it shows its own
\\ colour over anything, and since it's all EOR, the balls' drawing in between doesn't matter: off and on
\\ always leave the screen as the balls alone. A new spark keeps 0s, so it isn't EORed off first.
\\
\\ A spark's place is units (SparkX: from the well's left) and quarters (SparkXF), down likewise; its
\\ speed quarters of a unit a frame, signed. Each across table runs on into its down one, so one routine moves
\\ both, indexed by the slot and the slot + SparkSlots. The slots are the loader's tables, in its gaps
\\ (gendata.py), zeroed with them.

SparkSlots = GenSparkSlots

\\ Each frame, after the balls: every live spark off, moved (a step, 7/8 of its speed kept, rounded toward
\\ 0, then gravity's quarter down if it's on), and on, the last slot first; gone when its time's up, or past
\\ a wall or the floor. Only the slots under SparkTop: none higher is live.
\\
\\ Inputs:
\\     the sparks' slots
\\
\\ Outputs:
\\     SparkTop: past the highest still live
\\     A, X, Y: corrupted

.update_sparks
{
	ZA_AUTO2 ptr						; local: its byte column's first byte in the row (Y its even line)
	ZA_AUTO1 mask, top					; local: its pixel; past the highest still live, as found
	ASSERT (SparkSlots AND (SparkSlots - 1)) == 0, "a slot EOR SparkSlots is its down index, and back"
	ASSERT SparkY == SparkX + SparkSlots, "each across table runs on into its down one"
	ASSERT SparkYF == SparkXF + SparkSlots, "each across table runs on into its down one"
	ASSERT SparkVY == SparkVX + SparkSlots, "each across table runs on into its down one"
	LDA #0:STA top
	LDX SparkTop:BEQ none
	DEX
.slot
	LDA SparkLife,X:BEQ next
	LDA SparkKept0,X:ORA SparkKept1,X:BEQ off
	JSR at								; off
	LDA (ptr),Y:EOR SparkKept0,X:STA (ptr),Y
	INY:LDA (ptr),Y:EOR SparkKept1,X:STA (ptr),Y
.off
	DEC SparkLife,X:BEQ next
	JSR step							; across
	TXA:EOR #SparkSlots:TAX
	JSR step							; down
IF GenSparkGravity
	INC SparkVX,X						; (SparkVY): gravity
ENDIF
	TXA:EOR #SparkSlots:TAX
	LDA SparkX,X:BMI gone				; past a wall (past the left wraps to 128 or more)
	LDA SparkY,X:CMP #FloorLine:BCS gone	; or the floor (past the top wraps too)
	JSR at								; on
	LDA SparkX,X:LSR A:LSR A			; its pixel: the left, or the right
	LDA #&AA:BCC @+:LSR A:.@
	STA mask
	LDA (ptr),Y:EOR SparkEven,X:AND mask:STA SparkKept0,X:EOR (ptr),Y:STA (ptr),Y
	INY:LDA (ptr),Y:EOR SparkOdd,X:AND mask:STA SparkKept1,X:EOR (ptr),Y:STA (ptr),Y
	LDA top:BNE next					; (the first still live, from the top)
	INX:STX top:DEX
.next
	DEX:BPL slot
	LDA top:STA SparkTop
.none
	RTS
.gone
	LDA #0:STA SparkLife,X
	BEQ next

	\\ Its byte: its column's in its row, and its even line in that (the odd line's the next).
	\\ Inputs: X, a slot. Outputs: ptr, the column's first byte in the row; Y, the even line; A corrupted

.at
	LDY SparkY,X:LDA RowHi,Y:STA ptr+1
	LDA SparkX,X:AND #&FC:ASL A:STA ptr	; its byte column * 8
	TYA:AND #6:TAY
	RTS

	\\ A step, and 7/8 of the speed kept.
	\\ Inputs: X, a slot (across) or a slot + SparkSlots (down). Outputs: A, Y corrupted

.step
	LDA SparkVX,X:CLC:ADC SparkXF,X:TAY	; the speed and the quarters (2r + 3 at most: gendata.py asserts it's under 128)
	AND #3:STA SparkXF,X
	TYA:CMP #&80:ROR A:CMP #&80:ROR A	; / 4, signed, rounded down
	CLC:ADC SparkX,X:STA SparkX,X
	LDA SparkVX,X:BPL @+:CLC:ADC #7:.@	; / 8, rounded toward 0
	CMP #&80:ROR A:CMP #&80:ROR A:CMP #&80:ROR A
	EOR #&FF:SEC:ADC SparkVX,X:STA SparkVX,X	; (less it: + NOT it + 1)
	RTS
}
